text: >-
  Likelihood of Explosive Residue Transfer &

  Detectability on Synthetic Fibers

  TRAPPING IN

  TESTABILITY /

  TRANSFER

  FIBERS

  RECOVERY

  HIGH

  HIGH

  MEDIUM-HIGH

  HPLC

  Handling or proximity to detonation

  readily transfers particles to synthetic

  surfaces. Fingerprint-level and

  post-blast resides common.

  Nylon, polyester, and auto carpet

  (typically nylon or polyester blends)

  are porous and fibrous - particles

  Lodge between fibers and in the

  pile. Better retention than many

  smooth surfaces.

  Solvent extraction (acetone/methanol)

  + HPLC-UV or LC-MS recovers resides

  effectively. Nylon often shows higher

  recovery than cotton; polyester/auto carpet

  also workable. Detection at low ug/g to ng

  levels possible when properly sampled.

  Nylon

  Good-High

  Lower

  High recovery

  Polyester / Auto Carpet

  Cotton

  Lower

  Based on forestic studies of post-blast and handling resides (RDX, PETN,
  TNT-related compounds), Actual results depend on amount

  deposited, time, weathering, washing, and extraction method. Outdoor or
  heavily soiled carpet reduces likelihood.
